  dialogueLines:
  - Ah, a traveler... been a while since I've seen a fresh face around here.
  - The sand gets into everything, doesn't it? Even your thoughts.
  - Sit with me awhile, if you have time.
  - You know... this desert holds secrets. Treasures too. My people always knew about
    them. Always talked about going.
  - But talking... talking isn't doing, is it?
  - Fear? Comfort? Laziness? Pick one. We told ourselves 'next week' for twenty years.
  - Now look at us. Snakes crawling out of every hole. Funny how life works, isn't
    it?
  - 'Maybe. Maybe not. Here''s what I know: that treasure could''ve fed our children
    for generations. Instead, it fed our fears.'
  - "Tell me, young one\u2014when you see something you want, what do you do?"
  - That's... honest. Most people lie to themselves. Say they're 'being careful'
    when they're really just scared.
  - Nothing wrong with fear, mind you. It's what you do with it that counts.
  - If I could go back... No. No use dwelling.
  - "Just remember this: opportunity doesn't knock twice in the desert. Sometimes
    it doesn't knock at all\u2014it slithers right past you while you're deciding. "
  - Now go. Before more snakes come.
  typingSpeed: 0.01
